From: opencodecs <noreply@opencodecs.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] Emit JXL_DEC_FRAME_PROGRESSION for modular streams with Squeeze

The decoder's public C API gates JXL_DEC_FRAME_PROGRESSION emission on
FrameEncoding::kVarDCT in dec_frame.h:SetPauseAtProgressive(). That
gate predates the maturity of modular Squeeze flush support; the
TODO(lode) comment this patch removes acknowledges it should lift.

For a modular stream encoded with Squeeze applied
(JXL_ENC_FRAME_SETTING_RESPONSIVE=1 + effort high enough for the
encoder to actually invoke Squeeze), the LF group decode produces a
valid 1:8 downsampled pyramid level. ProcessDCGroup decodes the LF
layer with minShift=3; FinalizeDC() is a no-op for modular; the
existing FrameDecoder::Flush() path calls
modular_frame_decoder_.FinalizeDecoding() to undo the global Squeeze
transform and produce float pixels.

So everything past the gate works for Squeeze modular. This patch:

* Lifts the kVarDCT gate at SetPauseAtProgressive so modular frames
  can have progressive_detail_ set to kDC.
* Adds a Squeeze check at the emission site in ProcessSections, so
  modular streams without Squeeze (where Flush() would return
  zero/garbage) don't fire spurious events.

Behaviour by frame kind:

* VarDCT: unchanged. The kVarDCT branch of can_emit_dc_progression
  in ProcessSections matches the original gate.
* Modular with Squeeze: FRAME_PROGRESSION fires after FinalizeDC,
  JxlDecoderFlushImage returns the inverse-Squeezed 1:8 image.
* Modular WITHOUT Squeeze: no event fires. Decoder proceeds to
  FULL_IMAGE as before; callers fall back to full decode + slice.

The Squeeze detection runs after ProcessDCGlobal (which calls
DecodeGlobalInfo and populates the transform vectors), so the
transforms list is reliably available at the gate site.

Tested against libjxl v0.11.2 on macOS arm64.

Author: opencodecs maintainers
Upstream-status: not yet submitted

---
diff --git a/lib/jxl/dec_frame.cc b/lib/jxl/dec_frame.cc
index 04c3ee0..0238172 100644
--- a/lib/jxl/dec_frame.cc
+++ b/lib/jxl/dec_frame.cc
@@ -665,7 +665,17 @@ Status FrameDecoder::ProcessSections(const SectionInfo* sections, size_t num,
         pipeline_options));
     JXL_RETURN_IF_ERROR(FinalizeDC());
     JXL_RETURN_IF_ERROR(AllocateOutput());
-    if (progressive_detail_ >= JxlProgressiveDetail::kDC) {
+    // opencodecs patch: for modular streams, only emit the DC
+    // progressive event when a Squeeze transform is actually present
+    // — without Squeeze, FrameDecoder::Flush() returns a zero/garbage
+    // 1:8 buffer and any caller relying on a meaningful LF would see
+    // a black image. VarDCT always carries a valid DC pyramid, so
+    // the gate is no-op for it.
+    bool can_emit_dc_progression =
+        frame_header_.encoding == FrameEncoding::kVarDCT ||
+        modular_frame_decoder_.HasSqueezeTransform();
+    if (progressive_detail_ >= JxlProgressiveDetail::kDC &&
+        can_emit_dc_progression) {
       MarkSections(sections, num, section_status);
       return true;
     }
diff --git a/lib/jxl/dec_frame.h b/lib/jxl/dec_frame.h
index 26412fd..fe1f2d7 100644
--- a/lib/jxl/dec_frame.h
+++ b/lib/jxl/dec_frame.h
@@ -152,13 +152,13 @@ class FrameDecoder {
         // Therefore, can't correctly pause for a progressive step if there is
         // an extra channel (including alpha channel)
         // TODO(firsching): Check if this is still the case.
-        decoded_->metadata()->extra_channel_info.empty() &&
-        // DC is not guaranteed to be available in modular mode and may be a
-        // black image. If squeeze is used, it may be available depending on the
-        // current implementation.
-        // TODO(lode): do return DC if it's known that flushing at this point
-        // will produce a valid 1/8th downscaled image with modular encoding.
-        frame_header_.encoding == FrameEncoding::kVarDCT) {
+        decoded_->metadata()->extra_channel_info.empty()) {
+      // opencodecs patch: lift the FrameEncoding::kVarDCT gate. Modular
+      // streams written with RESPONSIVE=1 produce a valid 1:8 LF layer
+      // that JxlDecoderFlushImage exposes via the existing
+      // modular_frame_decoder_.FinalizeDecoding() path. The original
+      // kVarDCT-only gate predates that maturity — see TODO(lode) in
+      // upstream history.
       progressive_detail_ = prog_detail;
     } else {
       progressive_detail_ = JxlProgressiveDetail::kFrames;
diff --git a/lib/jxl/dec_modular.cc b/lib/jxl/dec_modular.cc
index e8dc17f..c272dcc 100644
--- a/lib/jxl/dec_modular.cc
+++ b/lib/jxl/dec_modular.cc
@@ -287,6 +287,25 @@ Status ModularFrameDecoder::DecodeGlobalInfo(BitReader* reader,
   return dec_status;
 }

+// opencodecs patch: detect whether this modular stream carries a
+// Squeeze transform. Called from FrameDecoder::ProcessSections after
+// DecodeGlobalInfo, where both transform vectors are populated.
+//
+// Squeeze can live in either of two places: the special-case
+// ``global_transform`` vector (RCT-only fast path) or the regular
+// ``full_image.transform`` vector. We check both — Squeeze is
+// effectively always in full_image.transform since the special-case
+// move only fires for an isolated RCT transform.
+bool ModularFrameDecoder::HasSqueezeTransform() const {
+  for (const auto& t : global_transform) {
+    if (t.id == TransformId::kSqueeze) return true;
+  }
+  for (const auto& t : full_image.transform) {
+    if (t.id == TransformId::kSqueeze) return true;
+  }
+  return false;
+}
+
 void ModularFrameDecoder::MaybeDropFullImage() {
   if (full_image.transform.empty() && !have_something && all_same_shift) {
     use_full_image = false;
diff --git a/lib/jxl/dec_modular.h b/lib/jxl/dec_modular.h
index 6081b52..325ff2d 100644
--- a/lib/jxl/dec_modular.h
+++ b/lib/jxl/dec_modular.h
@@ -128,6 +128,12 @@ class ModularFrameDecoder {
   void MaybeDropFullImage();
   bool UsesFullImage() const { return use_full_image; }
   JxlMemoryManager* memory_manager() const { return memory_manager_; }
+  // opencodecs patch: returns true iff the modular stream applied a
+  // Squeeze (Haar-style 1:8 LF pyramid) transform during encode.
+  // Used by FrameDecoder::ProcessSections to gate JXL_DEC_FRAME_PROGRESSION
+  // emission so we only fire the event when JxlDecoderFlushImage can
+  // actually produce a meaningful coarse-resolution image.
+  bool HasSqueezeTransform() const;

  private:
   Status ModularImageToDecodedRect(const FrameHeader& frame_header, Image& gi,
